# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. NEVER commit a filled-in copy.
# Deployed values are injected by Paperclip secrets / the host's env settings.
# A key that appears in this repo or in an issue comment is a leaked key.

# local | preview | production. Anything but `local` requires Langfuse keys.
APP_ENV=local
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Postgres ---------------------------------------------------------------
# These two placeholders are for a plain local Postgres only, where both are the
# same. Do not assume a deployed environment looks like this.
#
# Don't have one? `npm run db:local` starts a throwaway PostgreSQL 17 in
# `.local-postgres/`, applies every migration, seeds the event registry and
# creates the partitions, then prints the exact two lines to paste below. See
# ADR 0009. `npm run db:local:reset` throws it away.
#
# `?sslmode=disable` is not decoration. src/lib/db/pg-connection.ts reads an
# ABSENT sslmode the way the deployed pooler URLs need it read — encrypt, do not
# verify — so a bare local URL makes every `pg` caller demand TLS from a server
# that does not speak it and fail with "The server does not support SSL
# connections". The Prisma CLI is laxer, so migrations apply and the app still
# cannot connect, which is exactly the split that cost PRO-68 a day.
#
# Shared/deployed values come from Paperclip secrets and follow ADR 0005. They are
# TWO DIFFERENT ROLES, and that is the point — the app must never hold the one that
# can drop a table or disable an append-only trigger:
#   RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL -> role steamkid_runtime, port 6543,
#                   &pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1. DML only. No DDL. This is
#                   what application code gets.
#   MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL -> role steamkid_migrate, port 5432 (session mode; prisma
#                   migrate uses this). Owns the schema. Migrations and nothing else.
# `npm run verify:roles` proves the split still holds against a real database.
#
# Those two names, not DATABASE_URL/DIRECT_URL, because those two paths were
# already bound to the combined `steamkid_app` role and Paperclip will not
# overwrite an occupied config path (http_409). The old names still work as a
# fallback — that is what the placeholders below are — but the new name WINS when
# both are set, so a leftover injection cannot undo the split. `steamkid_app`
# itself was dropped on 2026-09-23; a URL still naming it is now refused with a
# message saying what to bind instead. See src/lib/db/connection-env.ts.
#
# Both deployed URLs carry `uselibpqcompat=true&sslmode=require`. Without the first
# half, pg 8.23+ reads `sslmode=require` as `verify-full` and the pooler's chain
# fails with "self-signed certificate in certificate chain".
#
# Do NOT use the `db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432` string the Supabase dashboard
# shows first. On the free tier it is IPv6-only, our runners have no IPv6 route, and
# it fails with a routing error that reads like an outage. See
# docs/adr/0005-postgres-access-path.md.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://steamkid:steamkid@127.0.0.1:55432/steamkid?sslmode=disable
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://steamkid:steamkid@127.0.0.1:55432/steamkid?sslmode=disable

# --- Auth.js ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Generate with: npx auth secret
AUTH_SECRET=

# --- LLM provider (server-side only) ----------------------------------------
# Gemini API. Must be an auth key on a BILLING-ENABLED project — the free tier
# trains on what you send it. See docs/adr/0004-llm-provider-gemini.md.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Langfuse (self-hosted; see docs/adr/0002-observability-and-privacy.md) --
# In a Paperclip runner these three arrive already injected in the environment.
# `npm run` is safe: Node's --env-file does NOT override a variable that is
# already set, so the blanks below lose to the injected values.
#
# `source .env.local` in a shell is NOT safe — it exports these as empty and
# blanks the injected credentials, after which every Langfuse call returns
# `401 Invalid authorization header. Confirm that you've configured the correct
# host.` That reads like a dead instance and is not one. Cost an hour on
# 2026-09-22 (PRO-64). Use `npm run <script>`, or export only what is missing.
LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=
# The secret is named LANGFUSE_BASE_URL; the SDK and this repo read
# LANGFUSE_BASEURL. src/lib/env.ts accepts either spelling — see
# trace-destination.test.ts.
LANGFUSE_BASEURL=

# Normally derived from APP_ENV. Set it when your traffic is synthetic and must
# not land in the same charts as real learners — a QA pass sets `qa`, so every
# trace it produces is filterable and droppable without touching real history.
# Lowercase alphanumerics with - or _; the `langfuse` prefix is reserved.
LANGFUSE_TRACING_ENVIRONMENT=

# --- Sentry -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The DSN is public by design. The auth token is not — build-time only.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
SENTRY_ORG=
SENTRY_PROJECT=
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# --- Internal cron endpoints (/api/internal/*) --------------------------------
# Shared secret for `/api/internal/db-partitions`, `sweep-sessions`, and
# `export-training-dataset`. Vercel Cron sends `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET`;
# set INTERNAL_CRON_SECRET to the same value shown in Vercel project settings
# (Settings → Environment Variables → CRON_SECRET). Min 16 characters.
# In APP_ENV=local with no value set, the check is skipped for local dev.
INTERNAL_CRON_SECRET=
